HDR swap chains for the renderer (renderer/README.md, Display). Applied after nri_agility_721.patch.

- NRISwapChain.h, SwapChainVK.hpp (HDR metadata): SwapChainDesc gets the content's peak and maximum frame-average
  luminance, sent with vkSetHdrMetadataEXT after the swap chain is created. NRI has no other way to reach
  VK_EXT_hdr_metadata, and the VkSwapchainKHR it would need is private.
- DispatchTable.h, DeviceVK.hpp: vkSetHdrMetadataEXT is loaded when the device enabled VK_EXT_hdr_metadata.
- SwapChainVK.hpp (format choice): BT709_G10_16BIT takes only EXTENDED_SRGB_LINEAR (scRGB) and BT2020_G2084_10BIT
  only HDR10_ST2084; without one, creation fails with UNSUPPORTED. Before, NRI fell back to any FP16 or A2B10G10R10
  format, for example FP16 with SRGB_NONLINEAR on NVIDIA's Wayland surfaces, which shows SDR. The chosen VkFormat
  and VkColorSpaceKHR are logged. BT709_G22_8BIT (SDR) chooses as before.
- ImguiInterface.hpp: ImGui writes alpha as premultiplied coverage (ONE, ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA), so the renderer can
  draw the UI into its own layer and composite it over a PQ frame. Over an opaque target (alpha 1) the alpha stays 1
  and the RGB result is unchanged.

